IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `maia-dates`

-- Motor Accident Injuries Act 2017 (NSW) -- the claim steps a person meets in Part 3 and Part 6 (Divisions 6.2-6.4):
-- the 28-day and 3-month steps for a claim for statutory benefits (s 6.13), the insurer's 4-week and 9-month notices
-- on liability (s 6.19), the 14-day and 7-day steps for the authority, medical certificate and certificate of fitness
-- the insurer asks for (ss 3.14, 3.15), what a certificate of fitness covers (s 3.15), and the 3-year step for a claim
-- for damages (s 6.14).
--
-- SEAT: the person injured in a motor accident (the claimant). Every exported question is one that person would ask:
-- "By when must I claim?", "Is my claim in time?", "By when must I claim to be paid from the start?", "By when must my
-- insurer tell me whether it accepts liability?", "Is my insurer taken to have accepted it?", "By when must I give my
-- insurer what it asked for, and can it suspend my payments?", "Does my certificate cover this day?". The insurer and
-- the Commission get no seat; their duties are encoded for what they mean to the claimant.
--
-- REGULATION. The Motor Accident Injuries Regulation 2017 (deposited beside the Act, version as at 22 September 2023)
-- is brought in where it sets this Part's numbers: cl 8A (weekly payments before a late claim, s 6.13(2)). It sets no
-- other period for ss 3.14, 3.15, 6.13(1) or 6.19, so the Act's own periods are used.
--
-- REGULATIVE RULES. Four deadlines are rules (PARTY ... MUST ... WITHIN ... HENCE ... LEST): the claim within 3 months
-- (s 6.13(1), with the late claim of s 6.13(3) under LEST), the insurer's notice on liability (s 6.19(1), (2), (4)), and
-- the claimant's compliance with an insurer's requirement (ss 3.14(2), 3.15(7)). Each is run by EVALTRACE inside an
-- exported question that takes only plain facts. Time is in days: time 0 is the day the period runs from, which is not
-- itself counted ("within N days after").
--
-- ANSWERS. As in maia-benefits.l4: JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no (including a period the text
-- fixes), NOTHING with a "NOTHING-kind" comment where it does not answer.
--
-- Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website (as collected by the Open Australian Legal Corpus on
-- 10 March 2025; version as at 1 April 2023; unofficial, possibly out of date). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for
-- public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Motor Accident Injuries Act 2017 -- claim steps`

§§ `The parties and the acts`

DECLARE `Claim party` IS ONE OF
    `the claimant`
    `the insurer`

DECLARE `Claim act` IS ONE OF
    `make the claim for statutory benefits`
    `make the claim for statutory benefits with a full and satisfactory explanation for the delay`
    `give notice whether it accepts liability`
    `comply with the requirement`

-- s 6.19(1), (2): which notice on liability.
DECLARE `The liability notice` IS ONE OF
    `the notice about the first 52 weeks after the accident`
    `the notice about the time after the first 52 weeks`

-- ss 3.14, 3.15: which requirement of the insurer.
DECLARE `The insurer's requirement` IS ONE OF
    `a medical certificate, or an authority for my treatment providers to give it information (s 3.14)`
    `a certificate of fitness for work, or a declaration about work (s 3.15)`

§§ `s 6.13 -- the 3-month and 28-day steps for a claim for statutory benefits`

-- s 6.13(1) "A claim for statutory benefits must be made within 3 months after the date of the motor accident to which
-- the claim relates." (The regulations may change the period; the deposited Regulation does not, so 3 months is
-- used.) The last day
-- is the same day of the month 3 months later, or that month's last day (fork F1).
GIVEN `the accident day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the 3 months after` `the accident day` MEANS `the accident day` `plus months` 3

@export By what day must I make my claim for statutory benefits (s 6.13(1))?
GIVEN `the day of my accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of your motor accident
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I claim statutory benefits` MEANS `the last day of the 3 months after` `the day of my accident`

-- s 6.13(2) "If a claim for statutory benefits is not made within 28 days after the date of the motor accident, weekly
-- payments of statutory benefits are not payable in respect of any period before the claim is made, unless permitted by
-- the regulations."
@export By what day must I make my claim for statutory benefits so that weekly payments can be paid from the start, not only from the day I claim (s 6.13(2))?
GIVEN `the day of my accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of your motor accident
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I claim to be paid weekly payments from the start` MEANS `the day of my accident` `plus days` 28

-- Regulation cl 8A(1) "payment of weekly payments of statutory benefits for a period before a claim is made is
-- permitted if (a) the claim is made within 3 months after the date of the motor accident ..., and (b) the claimant
-- provides a full and satisfactory explanation for the delay in making the claim." (3) an explanation is taken to be
-- full and satisfactory "if the insurer has not rejected the explanation within 14 days after receiving" it. (4) "This
-- clause does not apply to a motor accident occurring before 1 April 2023." (2) lists matters for the explanation
-- (awareness of the right, legal incapacity, illness or injury): the explanation is a judgment, asked.
GIVEN `the accident day` IS A DATE, `the claim day` IS A DATE, `an explanation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `weekly payments are payable for the time before the claim` `the accident day` `the claim day` `an explanation` IF
        (NOT (`the claim day` `is after` (`the accident day` `plus days` 28)))
    OR (    (NOT (`the claim day` `is after` (`the last day of the 3 months after` `the accident day`)))
        AND `an explanation`
        AND (NOT (`the accident day` `is before` (`the date` 1 4 2023))))

@export If I claim on this day, are weekly payments payable for the time before my claim, or only from the day I claim (s 6.13(2); Regulation cl 8A)?
GIVEN `the day of my accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of your motor accident
      `the day I make my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you made (or will make) your claim for statutory benefits
      `I give a full and satisfactory explanation for the late claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you claim more than 28 days after the accident: whether you give a full and satisfactory explanation for the delay (for example, you did not know of the right to claim, were under a legal incapacity, or were prevented by illness or injury); it is taken to be one if the insurer does not reject it within 14 days of receiving it
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Are weekly payments payable for the time before my claim` MEANS
    IF `weekly payments are payable for the time before the claim` `the day of my accident` `the day I make my claim` `I give a full and satisfactory explanation for the late claim`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 6.13(1) with (3): "However, a claim for statutory benefits may be made after the time required by subsection (1)
-- if the claimant provides a full and satisfactory explanation for the delay in making the claim, and either (a) the
-- claim is made within 3 years after the date of the motor accident, or (b) the claim is in respect of the death of a
-- person or injury resulting in a degree of permanent impairment of the injured person that is greater than 10%." Time
-- 0 is the day of the accident. The late claim is the LEST branch: it starts when the 3 months have passed; with
-- (3)(b) it has no outer limit (no WITHIN). s 6.2: an explanation is "full and satisfactory" only if it is a full
-- account and a reasonable person in the claimant's position would have been delayed the same: a judgment, asked.
GIVEN `the days in the 3 months` IS A NUMBER, `the days left in the 3 years` IS A NUMBER, `no outer limit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Claim party` `Claim act`
`s 6.13(1), (3) -- the claimant must claim within 3 months, or late with an explanation` `the days in the 3 months` `the days left in the 3 years` `no outer limit` MEANS
    PARTY `the claimant`
    MUST `make the claim for statutory benefits`
    WITHIN `the days in the 3 months`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST
        IF `no outer limit`
        THEN
            PARTY `the claimant`
            MUST `make the claim for statutory benefits with a full and satisfactory explanation for the delay`
        ELSE
            PARTY `the claimant`
            MUST `make the claim for statutory benefits with a full and satisfactory explanation for the delay`
            WITHIN `the days left in the 3 years`
            HENCE FULFILLED
            LEST BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "a claim for statutory benefits made more than 3 years after the accident, or after 3 months without a full and satisfactory explanation (s 6.13(1), (3))"

-- s 6.13(4) "In addition, a claim for statutory benefits under Division 3.4 in respect of an injury for which
-- compensation under Division 3 ... of Part 3 of the Workers Compensation Act 1987 has been payable may be made within 3
-- months after the compensation ceases to be payable."
@export Is my claim for statutory benefits made in time, or allowed as a late claim, if I make it on this day (s 6.13(1), (3), (4))?
GIVEN `the day of my accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of your motor accident
      `the day I make my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you made (or will make) your claim for statutory benefits
      `I give a full and satisfactory explanation for the delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you claim more than 3 months after the accident: whether you give a full and satisfactory explanation for the delay (a full account of what you did, knew and believed from the accident to the explanation, such that a reasonable person in your position would have been delayed the same)
      `the claim is for a death or for an impairment over 10%` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for a death, or for an injury with a degree of permanent impairment greater than 10%
      `the claim is only for treatment and care, and workers compensation for medical expenses has stopped` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is only for treatment and care (Division 3.4), workers compensation for medical, hospital and rehabilitation expenses (WCA Part 3 Division 3) was payable for the injury, and it has stopped being payable
      `the day workers compensation for medical expenses stopped` IS A DATE @desc If so: the day that workers compensation stopped being payable (any day otherwise)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my claim for statutory benefits in time` MEANS
    IF `the claim is only for treatment and care, and workers compensation for medical expenses has stopped`
       AND (NOT (`the day I make my claim` `is after` (`the day workers compensation for medical expenses stopped` `plus months` 3)))
       AND (NOT (`the day I make my claim` `is before` `the day workers compensation for medical expenses stopped`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 6.13(1), (3) -- the claimant must claim within 3 months, or late with an explanation` `the days in the 3 months` `the days left` `the claim is for a death or for an impairment over 10%`) 0 `the events`
        WHEN FULFILLED THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `the days in the 3 months` MEANS `the days from` `the day of my accident` `to` (`the last day of the 3 months after` `the day of my accident`)
        `the days in the 3 years` MEANS `the days from` `the day of my accident` `to` (`the day of my accident` `plus months` 36)
        -- the late-claim rule starts on the day after the 3 months (the WAITUNTIL below), so its WITHIN is what is
        -- left of the 3 years from then.
        `the days left` MEANS `the days in the 3 years` MINUS (`the days in the 3 months` PLUS 1)
        `the claim day` MEANS `the days from` `the day of my accident` `to` `the day I make my claim`
        `the events` MEANS
            IF `the claim day` AT MOST `the days in the 3 months`
            THEN LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `make the claim for statutory benefits` `the claim day`)
            ELSE IF `I give a full and satisfactory explanation for the delay`
                 THEN LIST (WAITUNTIL (`the days in the 3 months` PLUS 1)), (EVENT `the claimant` `make the claim for statutory benefits with a full and satisfactory explanation for the delay` `the claim day`)
                 ELSE LIST (WAITUNTIL (`the days in the 3 months` PLUS 1)), (EVENT `the claimant` `make the claim for statutory benefits` `the claim day`)

§§ `s 6.19 -- the insurer's notice whether it accepts liability`

-- s 6.19(1) "An insurer must, within 4 weeks after a claimant makes a claim for statutory benefits, give the claimant
-- notice ... stating whether or not the insurer accepts liability for the payment of statutory benefits during the
-- first 52 weeks after the time of the motor accident"; (2) "within 9 months ... after the first 52 weeks"; (4) "If the
-- insurer fails to notify the claimant in accordance with this section, the insurer is taken to have accepted
-- liability for the statutory benefits concerned." (5) the insurer may later deny, (6) and then cannot recover what it
-- paid on the acceptance. Sch 4 cl 16: the 2022 amendments to this section (Sch 1 [32], [33] of the amending Act) do not
-- apply to an accident before they commenced; the earlier wording is not deposited, so for such an accident the
-- answers are NOTHING (fork F6).
GIVEN `the notice` IS A `The liability notice`, `the claim day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the insurer's last day for` `the notice` `after a claim made on` `the claim day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the notice`
    WHEN `the notice about the first 52 weeks after the accident` THEN `the claim day` `plus days` 28
    WHEN `the notice about the time after the first 52 weeks` THEN `the claim day` `plus months` 9

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Claim party` `Claim act`
`s 6.19 -- the insurer must give notice whether it accepts liability` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the insurer`
    MUST `give notice whether it accepts liability`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the insurer` BECAUSE "no notice on liability in time: the insurer is taken to have accepted liability for the statutory benefits concerned (s 6.19(4))"

@export By what day must my insurer tell me whether it accepts liability for my statutory benefits (s 6.19(1), (2))?
GIVEN `the day I made my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you made your claim for statutory benefits
      `which notice` IS A `The liability notice` @desc Which notice. One of: "the notice about the first 52 weeks after the accident", "the notice about the time after the first 52 weeks"
      `the 2022 amendments apply to my accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your accident happened on or after the day the changes made by the Motor Accident Injuries Amendment Act 2022 commenced (the deposited text does not give that day)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`By when must my insurer tell me whether it accepts liability` MEANS
    IF `the 2022 amendments apply to my accident`
    THEN JUST (`the insurer's last day for` `which notice` `after a claim made on` `the day I made my claim`)
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the sources: the pre-2022 text of s 6.19)

@export Is my insurer taken to have accepted liability for my statutory benefits because it did not tell me in time whether it accepts liability (s 6.19(4))?
GIVEN `the day I made my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you made your claim for statutory benefits
      `which notice` IS A `The liability notice` @desc Which notice. One of: "the notice about the first 52 weeks after the accident", "the notice about the time after the first 52 weeks"
      `the insurer has given me that notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer has given you that notice, stating whether or not it accepts liability, in accordance with the Motor Accident Guidelines
      `the day the insurer gave me the notice` IS A DATE @desc If so: the day it gave you the notice (any day otherwise)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about (usually today)
      `the 2022 amendments apply to my accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your accident happened on or after the day the changes made by the Motor Accident Injuries Amendment Act 2022 commenced (the deposited text does not give that day)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my insurer taken to have accepted liability` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `the 2022 amendments apply to my accident`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the sources: the pre-2022 text of s 6.19)
           IF `the notice counts` AND (NOT (`today` `is after` `the last day`)) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (NOT `the notice counts`) AND (NOT (`today` `is after` `the last day`)) THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 6.19 -- the insurer must give notice whether it accepts liability` (`the days from` `the day I made my claim` `to` `the last day`)) 0 `the events`
               WHEN FULFILLED THEN JUST FALSE
               OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS `the insurer's last day for` `which notice` `after a claim made on` `the day I made my claim`
        -- a notice given after the day asked about has not yet been given on that day.
        `the notice counts` MEANS `the insurer has given me that notice` AND (NOT (`the day the insurer gave me the notice` `is after` `today`))
        `the events` MEANS
            IF `the notice counts`
            THEN LIST (EVENT `the insurer` `give notice whether it accepts liability` (`the days from` `the day I made my claim` `to` `the day the insurer gave me the notice`))
            ELSE LIST (WAITUNTIL (`the days from` `the day I made my claim` `to` `today`))

§§ `ss 3.14, 3.15 -- what the insurer asks for, and suspension (a situation: I am receiving weekly payments)`

-- s 3.14(2) "If a person fails to comply with a requirement under this section within 14 days (or other period
-- prescribed by the regulations) after the requirement is communicated to the person by the insurer, the insurer may
-- suspend payment of weekly payments ... during any period that the failure to comply continues. The person forfeits
-- his or her entitlement to weekly payments during the period of any such suspension." s 3.15(7) the same for a
-- certificate of fitness or declaration, "within 7 days, or another period prescribed by the regulations", "subject
-- to the Motor Accident Guidelines". The deposited Regulation prescribes no other period: 14 and 7 days are used.
GIVEN `the requirement` IS A `The insurer's requirement`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days to comply with` `the requirement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the requirement`
    WHEN `a medical certificate, or an authority for my treatment providers to give it information (s 3.14)` THEN 14
    WHEN `a certificate of fitness for work, or a declaration about work (s 3.15)` THEN 7

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Claim party` `Claim act`
`ss 3.14(2), 3.15(7) -- the claimant must comply with the insurer's requirement` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the claimant`
    MUST `comply with the requirement`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "the insurer's requirement not complied with in time: the insurer may suspend weekly payments while the failure continues, and they are forfeited for the suspension (ss 3.14(2), 3.15(7))"

@export By what day must I give my insurer the certificate, authority or declaration it asked for (ss 3.14(2), 3.15(7))?
GIVEN `what the insurer asked for` IS A `The insurer's requirement` @desc What the insurer asked for. One of: "a medical certificate, or an authority for my treatment providers to give it information (s 3.14)", "a certificate of fitness for work, or a declaration about work (s 3.15)"
      `the day the insurer told me` IS A DATE @desc The day the insurer communicated the requirement to you
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I give my insurer what it asked for` MEANS `the day the insurer told me` `plus days` (`the days to comply with` `what the insurer asked for`)

@export Can my insurer suspend my weekly payments on this day because I have not given it the certificate, authority or declaration it asked for (ss 3.14(2), 3.15(7))?
GIVEN `what the insurer asked for` IS A `The insurer's requirement` @desc What the insurer asked for. One of: "a medical certificate, or an authority for my treatment providers to give it information (s 3.14)", "a certificate of fitness for work, or a declaration about work (s 3.15)"
      `the day the insurer told me` IS A DATE @desc The day the insurer communicated the requirement to you
      `I have complied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given the insurer what it asked for
      `the day I complied` IS A DATE @desc If so: the day you gave it (any day otherwise)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about (usually today)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my insurer suspend my weekly payments for this` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `complied by then` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (NOT (`the day I am asking about` `is after` (`the day the insurer told me` `plus days` `the days allowed`))) THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`ss 3.14(2), 3.15(7) -- the claimant must comply with the insurer's requirement` `the days allowed`) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL (`the days from` `the day the insurer told me` `to` `the day I am asking about`)))
               WHEN FULFILLED THEN JUST FALSE
               OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the days allowed` MEANS `the days to comply with` `what the insurer asked for`
        -- "during any period that the failure to comply continues": once complied with, even late, no suspension.
        `complied by then` MEANS `I have complied` AND (NOT (`the day I complied` `is after` `the day I am asking about`))

§§ `s 3.15 -- what a certificate of fitness for work covers`

-- s 3.15(3)(b) a certificate certifies fitness "during the period, not exceeding 28 days, stated in the certificate";
-- (4) it may cover a longer period "if (a) the person giving the certificate states in the certificate the special
-- reasons ... and (b) the insurer is satisfied ... that the certificate should be accepted"; (5) "A certificate of
-- fitness for work is of no effect to the extent that it relates to a period that is more than 90 days before the
-- certificate is provided by the injured person to the insurer." Fork F15: a certificate stating more than 28 days
-- without (4) is read as good for its first 28 days, the rest NOTHING (the Act does not say it is void). A day outside
-- the stated period is not certified: JUST FALSE. "More than 90 days before" is a day 91 or more days before the day
-- the certificate is provided.
@export Does my certificate of fitness for work count for this day (s 3.15(3)-(5))?
GIVEN `the first day the certificate covers` IS A DATE @desc The first day of the period stated in the certificate
      `the last day the certificate covers` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the period stated in the certificate
      `the certificate states special reasons and the insurer accepted it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the certificate states special reasons for covering more than 28 days and the insurer is satisfied it should be accepted for those reasons
      `the day I gave the certificate to the insurer` IS A DATE @desc The day you provided the certificate to the insurer
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc The day you want the certificate to cover
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does my certificate of fitness count for this day` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the day I am asking about` `is before` `the first day the certificate covers` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the day I am asking about` `is after` `the last day the certificate covers` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the days from` `the day I am asking about` `to` `the day I gave the certificate to the insurer` GREATER THAN 90 THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the day number in the certificate` GREATER THAN 28 AND (NOT `the certificate states special reasons and the insurer accepted it`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (the text is silent on the effect of a certificate over 28 days without special reasons; fork F15)
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the day number in the certificate` MEANS (`the days from` `the first day the certificate covers` `to` `the day I am asking about`) PLUS 1

§§ `s 6.14 -- the 3-year step for a claim for damages`

-- s 6.14(2) "A claim for damages must be made within 3 years after the date of the motor accident"; (3) "may be made
-- after the time required by subsection (2) (a late claim) if the claimant provides a full and satisfactory
-- explanation for the delay". Whether the insurer or the Commission accepts the explanation (ss 6.14(5)-(7)) is the
-- next step, not encoded.
@export By what day must I make a claim for damages (s 6.14(2))?
GIVEN `the day of my accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of your motor accident
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I claim damages` MEANS `the day of my accident` `plus months` 36

@export Can I make my claim for damages on this day (s 6.14(2), (3))?
GIVEN `the day of my accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of your motor accident
      `the day I make my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you make (or will make) the claim for damages
      `I give a full and satisfactory explanation for the delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you claim more than 3 years after the accident: whether you give a full and satisfactory explanation for the delay (first to the insurer)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I make my claim for damages` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the day I make my claim` `is after` (`the day of my accident` `plus months` 36))) OR `I give a full and satisfactory explanation for the delay`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
